5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roscoe</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Matteson</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Morrow</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name><name><surname>Hickok</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Bushunow</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Griggs</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Qazi</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Kramer</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acustimulation wrist bands are not effective for the control of chemotherapy-induced nausea in women with breast cancer</article-title><source>J Pain Symptom Manage</source><year>2005</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>376</fpage><lpage>384</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15857741</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jpainsymman.2004.07.007</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Post-White</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kinney</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Savik</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Gau</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilcox</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Lerner</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Therapeutic massage and healing touch improve symptoms in cancer</article-title><source>Integr Cancer Ther</source><year>2003</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>332</fpage><lpage>344</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14713325</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/1534735403259064</pub-id></citation